title: Cap light client execution proof request processing time
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Introduce a capped WASM executor using epoch-based wasmtime interruption mechanism and use it for serving light client execution proof requests.

    The execution is bounded by 3 seconds per runtime call — plenty of headroom for legitimate requests. The limit is configurable via `--light-request-execution-timeout-ms` (`0` disables it).

    The capped executor compiles the runtime into its own engine, so the light client request handler pre-warms it off the request path: once at startup, and again on every runtime upgrade and once (warp) sync reaches the tip of the chain, driven by best-block import notifications.
